[6] Being aggrieved and dissatisfied with the award passed by the learned L.A Judge, the appellant has filed this instant appeal seeking the following reliefs :
"(i) Admit the appeal;
The Deputy Chief Engineer ... vs Smt. Usha Rani Debnath on 20 January, 2023 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/116248298/
2 (ii) Call for the records of Misc.(LA) 26 of 2014 from the Court of Ld. Land Acquisition Judge, Court No.3, West Tripura, Agartala (Sri A. Pandey);
(iii) Issue notice upon the respondents;
(iv) After hearing the parties, be pleased to allow this appeal by setting aside the judgment and award dated 08/08/2019 passed by the learned Land Acquisition Judge, Court No.3, West Tripura, Agartala (Sri A. Pandey) in connection with Misc.
(L.A) 26 of 2014;
(v) Any other relief and relives as your Lordship deem fit and proper having regards to the facts and circumstances of the case."
[7] Mr. Ashutosh De, learned counsel appearing for the appellant submits that the learned L.A Judge committed an error in determining the market value of the acquired land.
